---
export interface Props {
    href: string;
    ariaLabel: string;
}

const { href, ariaLabel } = Astro.props;
---

{/*
  A dog-eared page corner, in the style of an e-reader's curled page.

  Drawn as SVG rather than a CSS clip-path because the curl's free edge is a
  curve, which clip-path can't express. Both shapes live in one <svg> so the
  underside and the flap share the exact same crease line and meet seamlessly:
  the flap's closing `Z` and the underside's hypotenuse are the same diagonal.
  Everything below/left of the curl stays transparent, so the page itself shows
  through there — that gap is what makes the corner read as rolled rather than
  cut off.
*/}
<a
    href={href}
    target='_blank'
    rel='noopener noreferrer'
    aria-label={ariaLabel}
    class='group pointer-events-none absolute right-0 top-0 hidden h-16 w-16 cursor-pointer transition-[width,height] duration-500 ease-out hover:h-56 hover:w-56 lg:block'
>
    <svg
        viewBox='0 0 100 100'
        class='absolute inset-0 h-full w-full overflow-visible drop-shadow-[-3px_4px_5px_rgba(2,6,23,0.35)] dark:drop-shadow-[-3px_4px_6px_rgba(0,0,0,0.6)]'
    >
        <defs>
            <linearGradient
                id='corner-fold-paper'
                gradientUnits='userSpaceOnUse'
                x1='65'
                y1='35'
                x2='5'
                y2='95'
            >
                <stop offset='0' class='[stop-color:#ffffff] dark:[stop-color:#4a5872]' />
                <stop offset='0.35' class='[stop-color:#fdfcf7] dark:[stop-color:#3e4a60]' />
                <stop offset='0.72' class='[stop-color:#f1ede1] dark:[stop-color:#2e3849]' />
                <stop offset='1' class='[stop-color:#cfc9b4] dark:[stop-color:#1a212c]' />
            </linearGradient>

            {/*
              The shadow the lifted flap casts onto the revealed page. The
              gradient axis is perpendicular to the crease (the vector (32,-32)
              points from the diagonal toward the corner), so a stop's offset
              tracks distance from the fold line: darkest right at the crease,
              gone by roughly two-thirds of the way out. Painted as translucent
              black over the flat fill so the one gradient darkens both the light
              and dark fills without per-theme stops.
            */}
            <linearGradient
                id='corner-fold-crease'
                gradientUnits='userSpaceOnUse'
                x1='0'
                y1='0'
                x2='32'
                y2='-32'
            >
                <stop offset='0' stop-color='#000000' stop-opacity='0.4' />
                <stop offset='0.5' stop-color='#000000' stop-opacity='0.12' />
                <stop offset='1' stop-color='#000000' stop-opacity='0' />
            </linearGradient>

            {/*
              Two shadows rather than one: lifted paper casts a tight, dark
              contact shadow where it almost touches the page, plus a broad faint
              one from the light it blocks overall. A single feDropShadow can
              only be one or the other, which is what made the curl read as a
              flat sticker.

              Both are built from SourceAlpha and combined with feMerge, rather
              than chaining two feDropShadows — chaining would shadow the first
              shadow and paint the result over the flap itself.
            */}
            <filter id='corner-fold-shadow' x='-60%' y='-60%' width='240%' height='240%'>
                <feGaussianBlur in='SourceAlpha' stdDeviation='5' result='ambientBlur' />
                <feOffset in='ambientBlur' dx='-4' dy='5' result='ambientOffset' />
                <feFlood flood-color='#0b1220' flood-opacity='0.18' result='ambientColor' />
                <feComposite in='ambientColor' in2='ambientOffset' operator='in' result='ambient' />

                <feGaussianBlur in='SourceAlpha' stdDeviation='1.2' result='contactBlur' />
                <feOffset in='contactBlur' dx='-1' dy='1.5' result='contactOffset' />
                <feFlood flood-color='#0b1220' flood-opacity='0.45' result='contactColor' />
                <feComposite in='contactColor' in2='contactOffset' operator='in' result='contact' />

                <feMerge>
                    <feMergeNode in='ambient' />
                    <feMergeNode in='contact' />
                    <feMergeNode in='SourceGraphic' />
                </feMerge>
            </filter>
        </defs>

        {/*
          Pointer events live on the paths, not the <a>, which is why the anchor
          above is pointer-events-none. The anchor is a square, but the fold only
          fills the corner of it — leaving the square clickable meant the
          expanded fold swallowed clicks aimed at the theme toggle beneath it.
          Hover and activation still reach the anchor by bubbling up from these
          paths.
        */}

        {/*
          The next page, revealed where the corner used to be.

          Uses Tailwind's built-in `blue` palette rather than `primary`: in this
          project the primary-* scale is declared in a plain `:root` block, not
          inside `@theme`, so it exists as CSS variables but Tailwind never
          generates `fill-primary-*` utilities from it — the path would fall back
          to default black. blue-600/blue-800 are the same hexes (#2563eb /
          #1e40af) and do generate. Swap these for any Tailwind palette utility
          (e.g. fill-emerald-600) to recolour.
        */}
        <path
            d='M0,0 L100,0 L100,100 Z'
            class='pointer-events-auto fill-indigo-600 dark:fill-indigo-800'
        />

        {/*
          Shadow of the flap on that revealed page, clipped to the same triangle
          so it can't spill past the fill. pointer-events-none so hover still
          reaches the fill beneath it.
        */}
        <path
            d='M0,0 L100,0 L100,100 Z'
            class='pointer-events-none'
            fill='url(#corner-fold-crease)'
        />

        {/* The corner itself, curled over to show the back of the page */}
        <path
            d='M0,0 C1,38 5,70 16,84 C30,96 62,100 100,100 Z'
            class='pointer-events-auto'
            fill='url(#corner-fold-paper)'
            filter='url(#corner-fold-shadow)'
        />
    </svg>

    {/*
      The label is printed on the revealed page underneath the fold: it stays
      hidden until hover, then fades in as the corner opens — it never peeks at
      rest. The wrapper is a fixed size (matching the expanded fold, not the
      resting one) so the text holds one position through the whole animation
      instead of drifting as the fold grows. overflow-hidden clips the inner span
      to that box so a translate can never push it past the viewport and add a
      horizontal scrollbar; clip-path then trims it to the revealed triangle so
      nothing spills onto the transparent page. The text is rotated to run
      parallel to the crease, sitting evenly across the wedge at a fixed size
      that doesn't shrink with the fold.

      Flex-centered, then nudged toward the top-right — but only slightly:
      the real limit isn't the clip-path (which is generous), it's the paper
      curl's own cream fill underneath. White text turns illegible the moment
      it drifts onto that curl, which happens well before the straight
      clip-path edge does anything. That leaves only about a one-point margin
      on each axis above the offset a two-line label needs to clear the top
      edge in the first place — verified empirically, not derived, since the
      curl boundary is a bezier, not a line. Don't push this much further.

      Fade timing is asymmetric: the delay belongs to the fade-in only, so the
      label waits for the corner to open; on the way out it clears immediately,
      before the fold shrinks past it.
    */}
    <span
        class='pointer-events-none absolute right-0 top-0 h-56 w-56 overflow-hidden [clip-path:polygon(0_0,100%_0,100%_100%)] opacity-0 transition-opacity delay-0 duration-150 ease-out group-hover:opacity-100 group-hover:delay-200 group-hover:duration-300'
    >
        <span
            class='absolute right-0 top-0 flex h-full w-full translate-x-[15%] translate-y-[-10%] items-center justify-center'
        >
            <span
                class='font-handwritten rotate-45 whitespace-nowrap text-center text-[25px] font-medium leading-none text-white'
            >
                <slot />
            </span>
        </span>
    </span>
</a>
